 ## Overview
-Spherical Harmonics Vector Quantization (SH VQ) is a compression technique for 3D Gaussian Splatting that replaces per-splat SH coefficients with indices pointing to a shared palette of distinct SH vectors, reducing memory footprint at the cost of minor lighting artifacts [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [First-order Spherical Harmonics Distillation](9467-first-order-spherical-harmonics-distillation.md) by retaining full SH basis functions (rather than reducing to first-order) and from [Explicit Camera Jacobian Derivation](10077-explicit-camera-jacobian-derivation.md) by focusing on storage compression rather than gradient computation [S1, unofficial]. It is chosen when memory bandwidth or storage size is the primary bottleneck and view-dependent specular effects must be preserved better than simple color quantization allows [S1, unofficial].
+Spherical Harmonics Vector Quantization (SH VQ) is a compression technique for 3D Gaussian Splatting that replaces per-splat SH coefficients with indices pointing to a shared palette of distinct SH vectors, reducing memory footprint at the cost of minor lighting artifacts [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [First-order Spherical Harmonics Distillation](9467-first-order-spherical-harmonics-distillation.md) by retaining full SH basis functions (rather than reducing to first-order) and from [Explicit Camera Jacobian Derivation](10077-explicit-camera-jacobian-derivation.md) by focusing on storage compression rather than gradient computation [G]. It is chosen when memory bandwidth or storage size is the primary bottleneck and view-dependent specular effects must be preserved better than simple color quantization allows [S1, unofficial].
 
